      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 954,
      "costUsd": 0.008647,
      "pronunciationText": "Start by naming what can change. Let x metres be each side out from the wall, and y metres the side along it. The fence covers x, y and x, so two x plus y equals forty. That's the constraint, a fixed total that links the variables. The area is x times y. But y changes whenever x does, so we can't differentiate yet. Use the constraint to replace y. y equals forty minus two x, so ay equals x, times forty minus two x, which is forty x minus two x squared. Now the area depends on x alone."
    },
