      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 185,
      "outputTokens": 1435,
      "costUsd": 0.0130075,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the calculus. A prime of x is forty minus four x, which is zero at x equals ten, inside the domain. Earlier in the course, we found a global maximum by comparing every candidate. Here the ends aren't candidates, because they aren't in the domain. So compare ten with the limits at the ends. A of ten is two hundred, bigger than both, and there's only one stationary point, so the area rises to two hundred and then falls. That makes two hundred the global maximum. Now answer the question. The pen is ten metres out from the wall and twenty metres along it, with an area of two hundred square metres. And here's why the square loses. Each metre along the wall costs one metre of fence, but each metre out from the wall costs two, because there are two of those sides. So the best pen is longer along the wall."
    },
