      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 890,
      "costUsd": 0.008071,
      "pronunciationText": "Now a second problem. An open box is made from a square of card twenty-four centimetres wide. Equal squares of side x centimetres are cut from the corners, and the sides fold up. The height of the box is x. Each side of the base loses two squares, so the base is twenty-four minus two x, each way. So the volume is x, times twenty-four minus two x, all squared. For the domain, x must be positive to cut anything, and twenty-four minus two x must be positive to leave a base, so x is less than twelve."
