      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 149,
      "outputTokens": 1051,
      "costUsd": 0.0095335,
      "pronunciationText": "Expand first. V is four x cubed, minus ninety-six x squared, plus five hundred and seventy-six x. So V prime is twelve x squared, minus a hundred and ninety-two x, plus five hundred and seventy-six. Take out twelve and factorise, to get twelve, times x minus four, times x minus twelve. Twelve isn't in the domain, and it would leave no base, so reject it. At x equals four, V is four times sixteen squared, which is one thousand and twenty-four. Near both ends the volume shrinks towards zero, so that's the greatest volume. Cut four-centimetre squares, and the box holds one thousand and twenty-four cubic centimetres."
    },
