      "pronunciationText": "With x out from the wall and y along it, x y is fifty, so y is fifty over x, and the fencing is two x plus fifty over x, for x greater than zero. Its derivative, two minus fifty over x squared, is zero at x equals five. Near zero, and for very large x, the fencing grows without limit, so five gives the least. That's five metres by ten, with twenty metres of fencing. x equals five alone doesn't answer the question."
